table schizophrenia treated with long-acting risperidone for 1 year</article-title><source>Br J Psychiatry</source><volume>187</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16055823</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-ndt-4-919"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fowler</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Bettinger</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name><name><surname>Argo</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Paliperidone extended-release tablets for the acute and maintenance treatment of schizophrenia</article-title><source>Clin Ther</source><volume>30</volume><fpage>231</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18343262</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ndt-4-919"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gefvert</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Eriksson</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Persson</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Pharmacokinetics and D2 receptor occupancy of long-acting injectable risperidone (Risperdal Consta) in patients with schizophrenia</article-title><source>Int J Neuropsychopharmacol</source><volume>8</volume><fpage>27</fpage><lpage>36</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15710053</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14-ndt-4-919"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gharabawi</surname><given-names>GM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bossie</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhu</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>An assessment of emergent tardive dyskinesia and existing dyskinesia in patients receiving long-acting, injectable risperidone: results from a long-term study</a